# Architecture

This project uses a small Python package with a `src/` layout and the **{{ profile }}** profile.
Application code is independent of the generator that created this repository.

{% if profile == "minimal" %}The minimal profile keeps one direct entrypoint in `main.py` and is
intentionally free of speculative layers. When multiple unrelated capabilities begin to
accumulate, do not create global `services/`, `models/`, `repositories/`, or `utils/` buckets;
consider migrating to the module structure described in `docs/agent/standards/module-placement.md`.
{% else %}The `greeting` capability lives under `modules/greeting/`; domain and application logic
depend inward, while the service profile additionally places its console adapter in that module.
`bootstrap.py` composes the service, and `entrypoints/cli.py` is a thin driver. The structure is
framework-neutral and deliberately tiny.

Place pure capability rules in `modules/<capability>/domain/`, use-case orchestration in
`application/`, and external I/O in that module's `adapters/`. Driving interfaces belong in
`entrypoints/`; project-wide configuration belongs in `config.py`. Domain does not depend on
application or outer layers, and application does not depend on adapters or entrypoints.
`platform/` is reserved for technical infrastructure genuinely shared by multiple capabilities;
`shared/` is for a very small set of stable domain-neutral primitives. Create neither until needed.
The full decision tree is in `docs/agent/standards/module-placement.md`.
{% endif %}
